module ilcd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Central District of Illinois's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the
// manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: the
// sentencing hearing is scheduled no earlier than 70 days after the entry
// of a guilty plea or a verdict of guilty (C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 32.1(A)),
// a floor rather than a deadline; a complaining party seeks to resolve
// disputed sentencing factors through opposing counsel and the probation
// officer before the hearing, and the presentence report, statement of
// reasons and recommendation are sealed (Crim. L.R. 32.1(B)-(D)); a
// transcript may not be copied by the Clerk for 90 days and becomes
// publicly available electronically 90 days after filing if no redaction
// is requested (Crim. L.R. 49.12(C)); an unredacted document or reference
// list not filed is kept for one year after the case ends (Crim. L.R.
// 49.12(B)); a filer keeps an original bearing a non-filer's signature
// until one year after the judgment becomes final (Crim. L.R.
// 49.10(B)(3)); filings due on a day CM/ECF cannot accept them for more
// than one hour after noon are due the next business day (Crim. L.R.
// 49.6(B)(3)). Format (Crim. L.R. 49.2), electronic filing (Crim. L.R.
// 49.3 to 49.11), probation records (Crim. L.R. 57.2), appearances
// (Crim. L.R. 57.3) and forfeiture of collateral (Crim. L.R. 58.2) set no
// other period. Former Crim. L.R. 16.2 was abrogated effective September
// 13, 2021 and stays effective only for discovery produced on or before
// September 12, 2021, under an edition that is not vendored.
//
// The earlier C.D. Ill. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.

/// The defendant is arraigned (C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 12.1, 16.1).
event Arraigned()
/// An attorney's or a pro se party's email address, mailing address,
/// telephone or fax number changes after registering for electronic
/// filing (C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.3).
event ContactInformationChanged()
/// A party or non-filing signatory receives notice that a document has
/// been electronically filed (C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.10(C)).
event FilingNoticeReceived()
/// The court reporter files an official transcript (C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R.
/// 49.12(C)).
event TranscriptFiled()

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 12.1: a pretrial motion under FRCrimP 12(b)(3) is
/// filed within 21 days of arraignment or such other time as the presiding
/// judge sets. Other motions may be filed without regard to this deadline
/// (Crim. L.R. 47.1, Committee Comments 2024).
deadline pretrial-motions: 21.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 12.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(A): within 7 days after the arraignment the
/// United States Attorney and the defendant's attorney confer and comply
/// with FRCrimP 16; a declination of a requested disclosure is in writing
/// (Crim. L.R. 16.1(B)).
deadline discovery-conference: 7.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(A)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(C): if additional discovery or inspection is
/// sought, defense counsel confers with the Assistant United States
/// Attorney within 14 days of the arraignment, or such later time as the
/// presiding judge sets for pretrial motions; the request is in writing.
deadline additional-discovery-conference: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(D): a motion to compel additional discovery or
/// inspection, with a brief, is filed within 14 days of the arraignment, or
/// such later time as the presiding judge sets for pretrial motions; it
/// states that the conference was held, its date, the Assistant United
/// States Attorney's name and that agreement could not be reached.
deadline motion-to-compel-discovery: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 16.1(D)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.3: an attorney or pro se party registered for
/// electronic filing files notice of a change of email address, mailing
/// address, telephone or fax number within 14 days and serves it on all
/// other parties.
deadline contact-change-notice: 14.days after ContactInformationChanged() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.3"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.10(C): a party or non-filing signatory who
/// disputes the authenticity of an electronically filed document or its
/// signatures files an objection within 14 days of receiving notice of the
/// filing.
deadline authenticity-objection: 14.days after FilingNoticeReceived() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.10(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.12(C): a party files a Notice of Intent to
/// Request Redaction within 7 days of the filing of the transcript.
deadline redaction-notice: 7.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.12(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.12(C): within 21 days from the filing of the
/// transcript the parties file under seal a Motion of Requested Redactions
/// locating the material by page and line.
deadline redaction-motion: 21.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Ill. Crim. L.R. 49.12(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
